{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSemitones"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<bend-alter>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/alter"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend\/alter"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBendV5alterSdvp","title":"alter","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-alter element indicates the number of semitones in the bend, similar to the alter element. As with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the alter element, numbers like 0.5 can be used to indicate microtones. Negative values indicate pre-bends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"releases. The pre-bend and release elements are used to distinguish what is intended. Because the bend-alter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element represents the number of steps in the bend, a release after a bend has a negative bend-alter value,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a zero value."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend/alter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-alter element indicates the number of semitones in the bend, similar to the alter element. As with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the alter element, numbers like 0.5 can be used to indicate microtones. Negative values indicate pre-bends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"releases. The pre-bend and release elements are used to distinguish what is intended. Because the bend-alter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element represents the number of steps in the bend, a release after a bend has a negative bend-alter value,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a zero value."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSemitones"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/alter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend\/alter","role":"symbol","title":"alter"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSemitones":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsemitones","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSemitones","abstract":[{"text":"The semitones type is a number representing semitones, used for chromatic alteration. A value of -1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponds to a flat and a value of 1 to a sharp. Decimal values like 0.5 (quarter tone sharp) are used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"microtones.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLSemitones","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"title":"MXLBend","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend type is used in guitar notation and tablature. A single note with a bend and release will contain two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bend elements: the first to represent the bend and the second to represent the release. The shape attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguishes between the angled bend symbols commonly used in standard notation and the curved bend symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commonly used in both tablature and standard notation."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}